<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44654" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sollĭcĭtātĭo</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sōlĭc-</span></b> ), ōnis,
			f.
		sollicito. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Vexation</i>, <i>anxiety</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nuptiarum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>on account of</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 1, 5, 26</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An inciting</i>, <i>instigating</i>,
				<i>instigation</i> (good prose): omnium, Planc.
			ap. <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Fam. 10, 24, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Allobrogum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cat. 3, 9, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Diogenis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Clu. 19, 53</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sollicitationibus expugnari,</span>”
				<i>seductions</i>, <i>allurements</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 2, 15 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sollicitationibus periclitari,</span>”
				<i>to find by trial</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					G. 2, 8</span></i>
			 (dub.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
